claim.claim-text:
a catheter (302) having a proximal end portion (322) and a distal end portion (324);
a handle (3304) coupled to the proximal end portion (322) of the catheter (302);
a lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) releasably coupled to the handle (3304);
a release assembly configured to releasably couple the lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) to the handle (3304); and
a lock line (92) having a first end portion (92A) fixedly coupled to the lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310), a second end portion (92B) releasably coupled to the lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310);
wherein the second end portion (92B) is configured to be released from the lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) by release of the lock line handle (2310, 3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) from the handle (3304) via operation of the release assembly.

the lock line handle (3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) further comprises a shaft (3310D, 6310G) releasably coupled with the spool (3304I, 6310E);
the second end portion (92B) of the lock line (92) is captured between the spool (33041, 6310E) and the shaft (3310D, 6310G); and
release of the lock line handle (3310, 4310, 5310, 6310, 7310) from the handle (3304) allows the second end portion (92B) of the lock line (92) to be released from between the spool (33041, 6310E) and the shaft (3310D, 6310G)
